        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7beb73fb-5c09-3eb0-9f79-c26dbec5b8b5",
                "word": "burthen",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e57c447f-637f-42a9-afc7-5ad1bd4d47f2",
                        "entry_id": "7beb73fb-5c09-3eb0-9f79-c26dbec5b8b5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "burthens"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb377f15-87ec-37e1-8ebe-e061b6db5bd8",
                        "entry_id": "7beb73fb-5c09-3eb0-9f79-c26dbec5b8b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The tonnage of a ship based on the number of tuns of wine that it could carry in its holds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f7ba0a4-1eb0-47aa-ad21-43d49b01f7e0",
                                "sense_id": "cb377f15-87ec-37e1-8ebe-e061b6db5bd8",
                                "text": "[...] and thence to Calstock, a town on the Tamar, which is washed by the sea flowing through Plymouth Sound and Hamoaze, and which place vessels of 200 tons burthen can reach at spring tides—[...]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53427e15-f1c5-311d-8c68-7e15f63cea9d",
                        "entry_id": "7beb73fb-5c09-3eb0-9f79-c26dbec5b8b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Archaic form of burden."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0eb6f345-c5ae-47a6-a4c1-bf4ef9799747",
                                "sense_id": "53427e15-f1c5-311d-8c68-7e15f63cea9d",
                                "text": "Nor less, I trust,\nTo them I may have owed another gift,\nOf aspect more sublime; that blessed mood,\nIn which the burthen of the mystery,\nIn which the heavy and the weary weight\nOf all this unintelligible world,\nIs lightened:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c7e8278-2358-4435-8220-13ca3ded2b53",
                                "sense_id": "53427e15-f1c5-311d-8c68-7e15f63cea9d",
                                "text": "It was with a daughter of Mr Shepherd, who had returned, after an unprosperous marriage, to her father's house, with the additional burthen of two children."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f034da3-29f3-4640-96f9-1fe49d761964",
                                "sense_id": "53427e15-f1c5-311d-8c68-7e15f63cea9d",
                                "text": "In some cases the conquering state contented itself with imposing a tribute on the vanquished: who, being, in consideration of that burthen, freed from the expense and trouble of their own military and naval protection, might enjoy under it a considerable share of economical prosperity, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76cf2c65-0568-439e-83f0-d0b9a6f324c2",
                                "sense_id": "53427e15-f1c5-311d-8c68-7e15f63cea9d",
                                "text": "Bidding them grope their way out and bestir,\n[…] though the worst\nBurthen of heat was theirs and the dry thirst"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "715a107e-32a3-331d-97b2-aecbca613aaa",
                        "entry_id": "7beb73fb-5c09-3eb0-9f79-c26dbec5b8b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "rarely used musical tempo, meaning slow and ponderous (e.g. moving under a burden); similar to largo"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f29db437-03aa-3dd6-935f-b02470d20bdd",
                        "entry_id": "7beb73fb-5c09-3eb0-9f79-c26dbec5b8b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "a section of music with the tempo mark \\\"burthen\\"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
